nvdisplay: nv-platform: add tegra194-nvrm compatible

Add "nvidia,tegra194-nvrm" to the platform device match table so that
nvidia.ko can probe on Xavier (tegra194) platforms when a matching DT
node is present. Uses a unique compatible string to avoid conflict with
tegra-display-hub which claims "nvidia,tegra194-display".

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [platform-specific]
Signed-off-by: Mateusz Krawczuk <mateusz.krawczuk@cybrixsystems.com>

--- a/nvdisplay/kernel-open/nvidia/nv-platform.c
+++ b/nvdisplay/kernel-open/nvidia/nv-platform.c
@@ -1216,6 +1216,7 @@ const struct of_device_id nv_platform_de
 {
     { .compatible = "nvidia,tegra234-display",},
+    { .compatible = "nvidia,tegra194-nvrm",},
     {},
 };
 MODULE_DEVICE_TABLE(of, nv_platform_device_table);
